      2 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">طبّخ</span></b> , inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَطْبِيخٌ</span>, <i>It</i> (a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">حِسْل</span> [or young
lizard of the species called <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ضَبّ</span>]) <i>grew big;</i> syn.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَبِرَ</span>. (S. [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُطَبِّخٌ</span>.]) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <i>He</i> (a boy)
<i>became active, and grew up,</i> or <i>became a young
man;</i> (L, K;) <i>grew big;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَبِرَ</span>; (K;) <i>and
became intelligent.</i> (L.)

